# =============================================================================
# CO2 Monitor — .gitignore
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Written 2026-10-18 when this project first went into version control.
# =============================================================================

# ---- CREDENTIALS -----------------------------------------------------------
# The firmware resolves every credential through !secret. The real values live
# in the Home Assistant config's esphome/secrets.yaml, NOT in this repo. The
# esphome/secrets.yaml kept beside the firmware in a working copy holds dummy
# values so the configs compile; it is ignored all the same, because a file
# named secrets.yaml that is "only dummies" is one paste away from not being.
# A credential committed once survives in history, every clone and every fork.
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
*.secret
*.key

# ---- ESPHome build output ----------------------------------------------------
.esphome/
# Compile logs are point-in-time build output; the result they record is in
# README.md (Status), with the config_hash that identifies each build.
*.log

# ---- Watchdog harness build output -----------------------------------------
# gen.py regenerates sim.cpp from sim.cpp.in + co2-node-common.yaml on every
# run, and faults.py writes its fault copies and binaries to work/. Committing
# them would be a second copy of the firmware lambdas that could drift (R10).
harness/sim.cpp
harness/work/
*.exe
*.pdb
*.obj
*.ilk

# ---- KiCad generated / local ----------------------------------------------
*-backups/
# Per-user local project state — window layout, last-opened sheet. Not design.
*.kicad_prl
*~
*.bak
*.bck
*.kicad_pcb-bak
*.kicad_sch-bak
*.lck
fp-info-cache
\#auto_saved_files#

# ---- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.ruff_cache/

# ---- OS --------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
